{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785296520,"nonce":"vSxw235l9tYYEupeIuG8M6NmBSI=","title":"b4 review tui: editor CRLF stored verbatim in reply buffer","message":"Reported by Matthieu Baerts in https://lore.kernel.org/tools/b2c44799-85a9-4576-9aae-b43eb1092315@kernel.org/\n\nAfter editing a reply, reopening the reply view showed every line ending in ^M (carriage returns), with extra blank lines appearing in the email-mode view. Manually stripping the \\r characters in the editor fixed all views and the reply sent fine. b4 stores whatever bytes the editor writes without normalizing line endings, so a CRLF-saved buffer propagates through all downstream views and helpers.","files":null}]}